<title>USA: Seven bidders for U.S. Stockpile nickel.</title>
<headline>Seven bidders for U.S. Stockpile nickel.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were seven companies bidding for nickel in the latest U.S. Stockpile offering.</p>
<p>Thalheimer Brothers bid for 40,000 lbs at $3.21 per lb.</p>
<p>National Nickel Alloy bid for 40,000 lbs at $3.25.</p>
<p>BenMet bid for 500,000 lbs at $3.213.</p>
<p>Abbey Metal Corp bid for 40,000 lbs at $3.211.</p>
<p>Phoenixx International bid for 500,000 lbs at $3.26.</p>
<p>Allied Deals bid for 44,100 lbs at $3.292.</p>
<p>Keywell bid for three lots of 80,000 lbs at $3.232, $3.222, and $3.212 respectively.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
